      "content": "### 7.2.1.2.2 Data Packet Payload",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 276,
      "bottomRightX": 645,
      "bottomRightY": 314,
      "content": "The DPP section consists of 0 to 1024 bytes of data payload followed by 4 bytes CRC-32.\nCRC-32 protects the data integrity of the data payload. CRC-32 is as follows:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 135,
      "topLeftY": 328,
      "bottomRightX": 645,
      "bottomRightY": 482,
      "content": "- The CRC-32 polynomial shall be 04C1 1DB7h.\n- The CRC-32 Initial value shall be FFFF FFFFh.\n- CRC-32 shall be calculated for all bytes of the DPP, not inclusive of any packet framing symbols.\n- CRC-32 calculation shall begin at byte 0, bit 0 and continue to bit 7 of each of the bytes of the DPP.\n- The remainder of CRC-32 shall be complemented.\n- The residual of CRC-32 shall be C704DD7Bh.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "list"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 158,
      "topLeftY": 489,
      "bottomRightX": 666,
      "bottomRightY": 520,
      "content": "Note: The inversion of the CRC-32 remainder adds an offset of FFFF FFFFh that will create a constant CRC-32 residual of C704DD7Bh at the receiver side.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 542,
      "bottomRightX": 652,
      "bottomRightY": 572,
      "content": "Figure 7-10 is an illustration of CRC-32 remainder generation. The output bit ordering is listed in Table 7-2.",
